---
// /legal/terms - terms of use for what is actually deployed.
//
// The service being described is real and small: a free, unauthenticated,
// read-only set of static pages. The clauses below are therefore written to
// match the deployment rather than to look like a platform's terms - no
// accounts, no user content, no paid tier, no SLA, no data collection to
// license. Where the operator's legal identity is still an open question in the
// plan (section 15, question 1), the clause says so instead of naming a country
// that has not been decided.

import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import JsonLd from '../../layouts/JsonLd.astro';
import { patchLabel, snapshot } from '../../lib/page';
import { absoluteUrl, jsonLdWebPage } from '../../lib/seo';
import {
  CONTACT_EMAIL,
  CONTACT_ROUTE,
  FREE_TIER_TEXT,
  NON_ENDORSEMENT_TEXT,
  NOT_AFFILIATED_TEXT,
  OPERATOR_IDENTITY,
  SITE_HOST,
  SITE_NAME,
  TRADEMARK_TEXT,
  VERSION_LINE,
  riotVerificationNote,
} from '../../lib/legal';

const snap = snapshot();
const url = absoluteUrl('/legal/terms/', Astro.site, Astro.url);
const title = `Terms of Service - ${SITE_NAME}`;
const description =
  `${SITE_NAME} terms of service: a free, unauthenticated site of pre-computed League of Legends statistics, ` +
  'provided as is, with no warranty of accuracy, and not affiliated with or endorsed by Riot Games.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  patch={patchLabel(snap)}
  canonical="/legal/terms/"
  generatedAt={snap.generatedAt}
  active="/legal/terms"
>
  <JsonLd value={jsonLdWebPage(url, title, description)} />

  <article>
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p>
      <strong>{VERSION_LINE}</strong> These terms govern your use of {SITE_NAME}, served at{' '}
      <code>https://{SITE_HOST}</code>. By reading the site you accept them. They are short because the service is
      small: if a clause here does not describe something the site actually does, it does not belong on this page.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Who provides this service</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is provided by {OPERATOR_IDENTITY} It runs on the operator's own hardware, at the operator's own
      expense, and it is not monetised: there is no advertising, no sponsorship, no paid tier and no commercial
      relationship with anyone whose data or game it describes.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What this service is</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} publishes pre-computed League of Legends ranked statistics as static web pages. It is free, it
      requires no account, no login and no payment, and it has no paid tier. There is no user-generated content, no
      submission form and no comment system: you read pages, and that is the whole interaction.
    </p>
    <p>{FREE_TIER_TEXT}</p>

    <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      You may read, link to and cite these pages. You may share the address of an individual page, and quoting a figure
      together with its sample size is welcome. You may not:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>present this data as official Riot Games statistics, or as reviewed, verified or endorsed by Riot Games;</li>
      <li>
        crawl the site at a rate that degrades it for other readers, or attempt to bypass its availability limits,
        caching or rate limiting;
      </li>
      <li>resell the data, or a substantially unchanged copy of it, as a product of your own;</li>
      <li>
        re-publish it in a way that removes the sample size, the patch, the region or the notices on this page, because
        that turns a measurement into a claim about the game;
      </li>
      <li>use the site in a way that breaks Riot Games' own terms, including its policies on third-party products; or</li>
      <li>use the site to make automated decisions about people, including decisions about a player's skill.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Your data</h2>
    <p>
      There are no accounts and nothing to sign up for, so there is no profile to manage, export or delete. What the
      site's own servers record, and what your browser talks to in order to draw a page, is described in the{' '}
      <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The statistics are provided as is, without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any implied warranty
      of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose or non-infringement. They are aggregate measurements of a
      sample of matches, they carry sampling error that is reported alongside each rate, and cells below the publication
      threshold are withheld rather than estimated. Nothing here is a promise that a figure is complete, current or
      correct, and nothing here is advice about how to play, what to buy or where to bet. See the{' '}
      <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a> for the specific limits these numbers have.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by the law that applies to you, the operator accepts no liability for any indirect
      or consequential loss, or for any loss of profit, revenue, data, goodwill or opportunity, arising out of or in
      connection with your use of this site or your reliance on a figure it publishes - including, without limitation,
      decisions about what to play, what to buy or whether to place a bet.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site is provided free of charge, and the operator's total liability in connection with it is limited to the
      amount you have paid for it, which is nothing.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing in these terms excludes or limits any liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited, and nothing
      here affects mandatory rights you have as a consumer under the law of your own country of residence.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Availability and changes to the service</h2>
    <p>
      There is no service-level agreement and no guarantee of availability, correctness or continuity. The site is a
      hobby project on self-hosted hardware: it may be unavailable during maintenance, re-deployment or an outage, and it
      may be changed or withdrawn at any time without notice.
    </p>
    <p>
      Pages describe a snapshot. A page rendered for one patch keeps describing that patch after the next patch exists,
      and is not updated in place, so an old page is a record rather than a stale copy of a current one.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Intellectual property and Riot's rights</h2>
    <p>{TRADEMARK_TEXT}</p>
    <p>
      Champion names, numeric ids and icons come from Riot's Data Dragon static data, which Riot publishes for this
      purpose, and image requests go from your browser to Riot's own CDN rather than being copied into this site. The
      underlying match data belongs to Riot Games. What this project owns is its own aggregation: the counts, the
      derived rates, the confidence intervals and the pages that present them, together with the code and prose in this
      repository, which is published under the MIT licence.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Riot Games non-endorsement</h2>
    <p>{NOT_AFFILIATED_TEXT}</p>
    <p>{NON_ENDORSEMENT_TEXT}</p>
    <p>
      Riot's policies for third-party products require, among other things, a verified site and a visible notice of this
      kind. Where those requirements are not yet satisfied, this site says so rather than implying compliance: see the
      section below.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Riot's verified-site requirement</h2>
    <p>{riotVerificationNote()}</p>

    <h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are explicitly amendable. They are reviewed on a fixed cadence and whenever Riot updates its own
      policies, and the outcome of each review is recorded rather than assumed. A material change is published as a new
      version of this page with the effective date above; continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the
      amended terms.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the law of the European Union member state in which the operator resides, and the
      courts of that member state have jurisdiction over any dispute that is not one a consumer is entitled to bring
      locally. The member state is not named on this page because the operator's published legal identity is not settled
      yet: that is an open item, and naming a country before it is decided would be a false claim about which law
      applies, which is worse than a slightly general clause. Nothing in this clause deprives you of the mandatory
      consumer protections of your own country of residence, or of your right to bring proceedings there.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Contact</h2>
    <p>{CONTACT_ROUTE}</p>
    <p>
      Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. If your message is about a specific page, include
      its address: it names its own patch, region, queue, bracket and snapshot, which is everything needed to look up
      how a figure was produced.
    </p>

    <p>
      See also the <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, the <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a> and{' '}
      <a href="/about">how the numbers are produced</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
